  "interpretation": "Fixed candidate-pool evidence and fixed selected-item identity evidence are distinct causal claims. A fixed-selected-identity acceptance claim is valid only if the bank/pool/state/selector are bound, memory updates are frozen, every condition exposes the same selected memory IDs+digests and compiled-guidance digest, and receiver acceptance is the sole contrasted variable. A system may always make the weaker fixed-candidate-pool claim when per-item selection is implicit or unlogged."
